{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness","id":1530811,"title":"What if KotE was in Chronicle of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-14T06:56:47-08:00","id":1530811,"title":"What if KotE was in Chronicle of Darkness","content":"So, KotE originally start off as VtM asia supplement, but it's turn into it's own gameline, but what if KotE was in VtR? VtR have other Wicked Undead creature, so why not have Kuei-Jin be one of them? And in this case 'Kindred of the East' refer to them being like the Kindred, but they're mainly found in the east, and not literally being Kindred just in the East. Just rework that they can be found anywhere in the world, but they have the most influence in Asia, and not just East Asia, and India, their Clan are divergent evolution instead of convergent, and each of the 'Covenant' are based on The Dharma, but less oriental, and have the 1,000 Hell be part of the Underworld that connect to Inferno, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T07:56:08-08:00","id":1530816,"title":"","content":"Because Spontaneous Rising is a thing in Requiem, so were animalistic undead like the Gui Ren first rise as, Wicked Dead calls them larvae and they may evolve into full vampires under another's tutelage/domestication if that is the tamer's actual intent. Not to mention the matter of &quot;clan as dharma&quot; that appears in Ancient Mysteries, Ancient Bloodlines &amp; 1000 Years of Night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Within the context of Requiem the &quot;Cathayan&quot;/&quot;Kuei-Jin&quot;/Gui Ren could exist fine, but there's no sense or reason in them being an &quot;other&quot; so to speak, they might as well be kindred already, because many of the things that made them different from Cainites <b>are </b>part and parcel of the kindred condition in Requiem, though not exactly general knowledge for the average neonate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T08:15:56-08:00","id":1530819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530816#post1530816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Spontaneous Rising is a thing in Requiem, so were animalistic undead like the Gui Ren first rise as, Wicked Dead calls them larvae and they may evolve into full vampires under another's tutelage/domestication if that is the tamer's actual intent. Not to mention the matter of &quot;clan as dharma&quot; that appears in Ancient Mysteries, Ancient Bloodlines &amp; 1000 Years of Night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Within the context of Requiem the &quot;Cathayan&quot;/&quot;Kuei-Jin&quot;/Gui Ren could exist fine, but there's no sense or reason in them being an &quot;other&quot; so to speak, they might as well be kindred already, because many of the things that made them different from Cainites <b>are </b>part and parcel of the kindred condition in Requiem, though not exactly general knowledge for the average neonate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically I feel this is lacking, admittedly i have been thinking about this, how would I drop the &quot;of the east&quot; and &quot;kindred&quot; part of KotE ...<br /> <br /> The Hungry Dead have literally escaped Hell, so 1) they know what it is to die and get a second chance, thus have something in common with Sin-eaters, they also think they know what the afterlife holds (and it isn't the Underworld). 2) they have been tormented and suffered for unknown amount of time, by presumably impossible powerful entities which may want them back, thus they have something in common with Changelings.<br /> <br /> So I would make them a new splatt, with no relationship to the Strix (and Dis) and instead another Lower Depth. My only question would be Duat or the Inferno, and I don't know half enough about either.<br /> <br /> Second I would not write an &quot;of the east&quot; book, because i am not from Asia, whether it be East Asia, South Asia, or South East Asia... But for more on that see: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nKic0LVGfC4\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/nKic0LVGfC4</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T09:20:31-08:00","id":1530827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530819#post1530819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thematically I feel this is lacking, admittedly i have been thinking about this, how would I drop the &quot;of the east&quot; and &quot;kindred&quot; part of KotE ...<br /> <br /> The Hungry Dead have literally escaped Hell, so 1) they know what it is to die and get a second chance, thus have something in common with Sin-eaters, they also think they know what the afterlife holds (and it isn't the Underworld). 2) they have been tormented and suffered for unknown amount of time, by presumably impossible powerful entities which may want them back, thus they have something in common with Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could look into Darklings and some of the Lost themselves - though not the base assumption for changelings, i remember at least one of the books bringing up the matter of either Lost or fetches as undead. The fact <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Fairest\" target=\"_blank\">Fairest</a> may include gandharvas &amp; dragons already opens up room for the idea of kami or the lords of the 10.000 hells as True Fae.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530819#post1530819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I would make them a new splatt, with no relationship to the Strix (and Dis) and instead another Lower Depth. My only question would be Duat or the Inferno, and I don't know half enough about either.</div> </div> </div> </div>IF one goes with the - quite hasty, might be said - assumption that all kindred come from the intervention of the Strix. The Nosferatu book gives hints connecting to the Zmai in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Predators#Chapter_Four:_Horrors_of_an_Ancient_Age\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Skinchangers\" target=\"_blank\">Skinchangers</a> speaks of the Kanaima risen from death to wreak vengeance upon the living with the tools and form gifted by the Jaguar, everything involving the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sta-Au\" target=\"_blank\">Sta-Au</a> and their mythic Land of Worms oozes hints of the Hellminth from <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Summoners\" target=\"_blank\">Summoners</a>, if memory tricks me not.<br /> <br /> Vampires are a morass of manyfold origins sprung from a patchwork of corpses, curses, magical fallout of varied sorts, all glued and fueled by the spilling of blood. They are repeating messes of ill-fate and synchronicity doing weird things to dead humans across the ages. Everything else is the remnants of humanity trying to attach an excess of meaning with mythology and religion.<br /> <br /> Damn, the matter of the nature of Strix is just as debatable as their supposed role in creating all kindred - there's evidence some individuals or groups might be collating under the same label beings that not exactly belong. Like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_mole\" target=\"_blank\">golden moles</a> who, name and superficial niche-based physical similarities notwithstanding, are in fact <i><b>much closer to elephants</b></i> in actual lineage and quite distinct from true moles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, ask yourself what you want to do different really and why you need or not a new splat.<br /> <br /> Ah, almost forgot - Mythologies does bring up the Sleep of Ages as far more than mere dreams and nightmares, but a spirit realm from which kindred come and go, with dangers its own like having one body's stolen by other dead, twisted in mind, memory and blood by torturing demons or escaping only to be pursued by entities in the form of punishment devils or death gods from a thousand religions, among other bits. Fun read that unfortunately never got the degree of fleshing out it probably merited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2024, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T10:34:21-08:00","id":1530829,"title":"","content":"I think if I were going to do KotE in CofD, there are two patches I would consider, one is to make the Kuei Jin a splat or night horror thing world wide. This likely emphasizes the ties to the Kindred. <br /> <br /> The other option I would consider is putting more emphasis on &quot;the East&quot;. It could be a localized and maybe time specific phenomenon with influences from Requiem and Sin Eaters ala Dark Eras or even a strand of the Contagion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T17:24:08-08:00","id":1530855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530827#post1530827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are a morass of manyfold origins sprung from a patchwork of corpses, curses, magical fallout of varied sorts, all glued and fueled by the spilling of blood..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they could entirely be another convergent evolution towards the vsmpiric form. But I want to get rid of the Kindred part aswell as the &quot;of the east&quot; part.<br /> <br /> My version might map better onto the Endless template from Mummy. (In fact I might start with a minor template rather than a full splatt, as it is more likely I will actually finish the project).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T17:39:39-08:00","id":1530856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530829#post1530829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if I were going to do KotE in CofD, there are two patches I would consider, one is to make the Kuei Jin a splat or night horror thing world wide. This likely emphasizes the ties to the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, a number of things that made the &quot;Kuei Jin&quot; a separate splat in WoD are already acceptable though uncommon options/alternate &quot;systems&quot; within the kindred condition, plus 2nd edition throws some thing into perspective by reinforcing out many &quot;clans&quot; are actually composed of several groups of beings with different origins through the ages and multiple parts of the world, but would prey upon each other or merge while acquiring qualities and learning tricks from each other.<br /> <br /> Plus, things are not exactly static when it comes to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jiang_Shi_(Night_Horrors)\" target=\"_blank\">wicked dead</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jiang_Shi_(clan)\" target=\"_blank\">kindred</a>, must be said. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Mekhet in their original form, according to their own clanbook, were possibly closer to garbage-sale mummies than vampires but adapted by interaction, exchange and contamination - at least according to one origin tale, the PoV character ended up having a vision that gave hints of something even older, connected to cavemen and eldritch shadow beasts, for example. And then there were the Grettir, who were closer to zombies or risen, but would later be absorbed into the Mekhet, if the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Norvegi\" target=\"_blank\">Norvegi</a> serve as evidence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530829#post1530829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other option I would consider is putting more emphasis on &quot;the East&quot;. It could be a localized and maybe time specific phenomenon with influences from Requiem and Sin Eaters ala Dark Eras or even a strand of the Contagion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also worth mentioning, Requiem 2e gives some tidbits implying that, while much better known through legends from China and neighboring countries culturally influenced by it, quite similar if not exactly the same monster might have spawned in other parts of the world under different names by their own circunstances unrelated to each other.<br /> <br /> So, the biggest issue i see is that much of what made KotE unique in relation to Masquerade is not quite unique, if at all, when it comes to Requiem, that concept-wise has room to cover both bases under the same label.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530855#post1530855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they could entirely be another convergent evolution towards the vsmpiric form. But I want to get rid of the Kindred part aswell as the &quot;of the east&quot; part.<br /> <br /> My version might map better onto the Endless template from Mummy. (In fact I might start with a minor template rather than a full splatt, as it is more likely I will actually finish the project).</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a strange pick, imho, from what i know about both splats, i dare say the Lost's dynamic with the True Fae feels much closer in spirit to the Gui Ren's relations and interactions with the Yomi Kings and their agents than anything like the Cursed's with the Judges - thought i'll be the first to admit to being no MtC connoiseur, so who knows.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it sounds like something only <i>very </i>distantly related in any way, form or spirit to KotE, if at all, no offense. But well, do whatever rocks your boat and good luck with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2024, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T18:08:49-08:00","id":1530857,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2024, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T20:38:36-08:00","id":1530862,"title":"","content":"I think drawing from Mummy allow the idea of &quot;escaped from hell&quot; as a more literal concept.<br /> Knowing how the judges work, the demons of duat and duat itself work, the comparison can be made.<br /> In this case our new Kuei-Jin would be souls that dodged judgement and escaped duat back into their dead bodies, I imagine now they hunger for Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Ironically, it feels like a possible type of antagonist for MtC, though perhaps a bit similar if weaker in execution to Shuankhsen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T02:23:27-08:00","id":1530881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530856#post1530856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a strange pick, imho, from what i know about both splats, i dare say the Lost's dynamic with the True Fae feels much closer in spirit to the Gui Ren's relations and interactions with the Yomi Kings and their agents than anything like the Cursed's with the Judges - thought i'll be the first to admit to being no MtC connoiseur, so who knows.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it sounds like something only <i>very </i>distantly related in any way, form or spirit to KotE, if at all, no offense. But well, do whatever rocks your boat and good luck with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you misunderstood, the Endless examples in Mummy core are:<br /> <br /> Blood bathers - who gain their immortality from bathing in the blood of their victims<br /> Body thieves - who have some mechanism to jump to a new (younger) body<br /> The Reborn - who are just reincarnations, keeping some memories intact, may require some ritual or quest to acquire their full memories.<br /> And the Eternals - who are pretty much Dorian Gray style immortals, anchored to a specific object.<br /> <br /> Then there are patchwork people, the Purified, and maybe one more.<br /> <br /> Thematically, they are all linked to Mummy only in that they make great NPCs as either antagonist/ally - because Mummy's relationship with memory is odd, and having someone in the party who can exist across time periods is useful (even if they have a new body).<br /> <br /> But mechanically they are a broad category of immortals which are mostly distinct from Kindred from not being undead (which would not be an issue for me).<br /> <br /> The question is socially and politically, how do they interact with Kindred society. What would other kindred consider acceptable, do you need a clan? (Not being able to embrace is one of the features of KotE) Would they be able to join a covenant? (KotE only had their Path like Dharmas, iirc, which might map to distinct covenants)?<br /> <br /> What else defines Kindred? The Banes? Their Cultue/social position (ie members of a Coteries/city-wide organisation)?<br /> <br /> Like I said, thematically I would go with themes of suffering, finding your place in the world, and trauma (from Lost) along with themes of second chances, and knowledge of the afterlife (from Geist), and not make a game which is thematically similar to Requiem.<br /> <br /> Also, not sure which Lower Depth to associate them with. Dis, the Inferno and Duat are the three I know anything about, I would not link them to Arcadia - there is already a whole game for that.<br /> <br /> But yeah, having a splatt (or even starting with a mini-template based on The Endless) and then asking where does fit in your game.<br /> <br /> How would the local vampire community interact with them? Would they join/form a Geist Krewe? Would they find safety within a changeling court? (Building powers based on Demonic contracts?) Would the local Mummy faction like another type of immortal pro/an-tagonist?<br /> <br /> In theory, with their shape-shifting power a KotE could join a Forsaken Pack. Learn Pack Rites, and develop shamanistic magic (hoping that binding/abjuring and understanding summoning magic can keep any Demons away).<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess under motivation, what I have is, what makes this concept different from Kindred (and the wicked dead/Revenants) because that is always that interested my about KotE.<br /> <br /> Making all different monsters of the night just be kindred is actually really boring to me - though I see why they went with &quot;not all kindred&quot; descend from one true source of power, as a way to make it distinct from VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  added motivation 02-15-2024, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T08:38:08-08:00","id":1530904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530881#post1530881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, you misunderstood, the Endless examples in Mummy core are:<br /> <br /> Blood bathers - who gain their immortality from bathing in the blood of their victims<br /> Body thieves - who have some mechanism to jump to a new (younger) body<br /> The Reborn - who are just reincarnations, keeping some memories intact, may require some ritual or quest to acquire their full memories.<br /> And the Eternals - who are pretty much Dorian Gray style immortals, anchored to a specific object.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, i keep forgetting that the contents of Immortals as a whole is not quite a Blue Book anymore, having been subsumed in part or wholy into MtC mythos.<br /> Goes to show how slight is my familiarity with the line as a whole. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (That and my own experience of once using Immortals and specially the Purified as a stepping stone for Collection of Heroes, a hybrid Hunter: the Vigil-Scion: Ragnarok chronicle, i guess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <br /> You clearly have a very well fleshed out idea of what blend of elements from KotE you want to emphasize, tinker with and how to bring them into a whole new perspective, so more power to it, have fun with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530881#post1530881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I guess under motivation, what I have is, what makes this concept different from Kindred (and the wicked dead/Revenants) because that is always that interested my about KotE.<br /> <br /> Making all different monsters of the night just be kindred is actually really boring to me - though I see why they went with &quot;not all kindred&quot; descend from one true source of power, as a way to make it distinct from VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not like all night critters have to be kindred indeed, it all depends on particular combinations of themes what splat to use, adapt or ignore and you decided to focus on something else altogether that i had failed to see, due to limited experience with MtC and my own experiences (and bias toward) KotE, i suspect.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T09:58:56-08:00","id":1530909,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I am glad they included them in 2e MtC since they were likely not going to get approved for their own book.<br /> <br /> But the minor template for Immortals isn't particularly deeply associated with Mummys or their mythology.<br /> <br /> I like this conversation to see what other ideas people have, and where the best can be taken or improved. I definitely like my direction, but I haven't had a chance to read about the Inferno yet (or enough about Duat, not sure about Dis).<br /> <br /> If the Hell they return from isn't Arcadia, or the Underworld, where else might it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T19:02:57-08:00","id":1530941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530909#post1530909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Hell they return from isn't Arcadia, or the Underworld, where else might it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Inferno? Their soul somehow got send into Inferno instead of the Underworld, and they manage to escape it's because it's wasn't meant to be where the soul go?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T00:39:25-08:00","id":1530953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530941#post1530941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Inferno? Their soul somehow got send into Inferno instead of the Underworld, and they manage to escape it's because it's wasn't meant to be where the soul go?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going to read up on the Inferno, but I think that works.<br /> <br /> Since we aren't told where souls go (except maybe those that belong to the judges in Mummy?) I feel like they might be 'supposed' to do something.<br /> <br /> The major difference between this idea and Changeling is, the Hungry Dead went to Hell, but they deserved it (or at least think they did). In fact, it doesn't matter if you use the rules for Kindred or not, writing a character who rises from the dead -without being sired - after being in hell, but thinks she deserved it. Makes for an interesting Kindred.<br /> <br /> In that case she likely thinks the Beast is am entity which comes from Hell and used her to escape... Or?? Is there a better interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T00:45:36-08:00","id":1530955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530953#post1530953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case she likely thinks the Beast is am entity which comes from Hell and used her to escape... Or?? Is there a better interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for Inferno I think that is a pretty good interpretation, since The Inferno book is about people who are claim by Inferno Demon.<br /> <br /> Kuei-jin in this case would be Inferno version of The Bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T01:27:23-08:00","id":1530960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530955#post1530955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for Inferno I think that is a pretty good interpretation, since The Inferno book is about people who are claim by Inferno Demon.<br /> <br /> Kuei-jin in this case would be Inferno version of The Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could model them after the Bound, but the Geist has an intrinsic connection to the Underworld (which can actually be visited and people regularly return from) whereas the Infernalist likely lack that...<br /> <br /> You could also likely model them with the Deviant rules if you wanted, I think their is a bound like 'alien entity' option.<br /> <br /> But I am assuming here we are modelling them as regular kindred, who happened to awaken without a sire (which is already a thing) and have to explain what their Beast is. That is, it acts like the Beast in Vampire, but they have a different explaination as to what it is ...<br /> <br /> Would they be more likely to join the Ordo an attempt to control their Demon? Or the Crone and embrace it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T04:57:09-08:00","id":1530970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530960#post1530960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But I am assuming here we are modelling them as regular kindred, who happened to awaken without a sire (which is already a thing) and have to explain what their Beast is. That is, it acts like the Beast in Vampire, but they have a different explaination as to what it is ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they shouldn't really be connected to the Kindred, more than a Being that suck life energy out of people, The 'Kindred' part of 'Kindred of the East', should be more symbolic than literal.<br /> <br /> I would change their hated of the Kindred, they don't hate the kindred, they just hate to be confuse with as one of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> I think the Kuei-Jin is unique enough on their own to be a seperate splat from the Kindred, but have enough connection to them that they are confuse with the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T06:10:16-08:00","id":1530972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530955#post1530955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kuei-jin in this case would be Inferno version of The Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be a really interesting take.I would love to see it if you go that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T06:20:39-08:00","id":1530974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530970#post1530970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they shouldn't really be connected to the Kindred, more than a Being that suck life energy out of people, The 'Kindred' part of 'Kindred of the East', should be more symbolic than literal.<br /> <br /> I would change their hated of the Kindred, they don't hate the kindred, they just hate to be confuse with as one of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> I think the Kuei-Jin is unique enough on their own to be a seperate splat from the Kindred, but have enough connection to them that they are confuse with the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any particular reason for keeping them separate beside &quot;they were in WoD&quot;? Because as i said before, a lot of what made them unique back in WoD is part &amp; parcel of the deep lore in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T06:25:46-08:00","id":1530975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530974#post1530974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any particular reason for keeping them separate beside &quot;they were in WoD&quot;? Because as i said before, a lot of what made them unique back in WoD is part &amp; parcel of the deep lore in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's perfectly acceptable for them not to be kindred. There are more things that go bump in the night and all. Heck, who knows, maybe in a few hundred or a thousand years, they might become kindred, that doesn't mean they have to be that way now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T09:00:02-08:00","id":1530981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530972#post1530972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that would be a really interesting take.I would love to see it if you go that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think taking them closer to the Bound but with a Demonic entity instead of a Geist would be an odd direction.<br /> <br /> I am not planning to go that way at least; I am definitely more pulled toward a Lost look-a-like. But with less emphasis on the mental Health and more on redemption.<br /> <br /> Which I think is a lot harder to focus on when you escaped by doing a deal to let an actual demon out of hell. Presumably that demon would have some motivation beyond merely experiencing the material world... I think I will be including Demons/temptation as a theme, but not giving the Returned personal Demons as characters with their own goals, like the Bound Geists in Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T11:11:37-08:00","id":1530992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1530981#post1530981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not planning to go that way at least;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's perfectly fine, perhaps the person I was replying to is interested in going that direction. There's more than enough room for multiple takes on the same concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T18:01:06-08:00","id":1531156,"title":"","content":"In my mind, I always thought Geist: Sin-Eaters = KotE. But, I've never read Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T00:56:30-08:00","id":1531177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530811-what-if-kote-was-in-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1531156#post1531156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my mind, I always thought Geist: Sin-Eaters = KotE. But, I've never read Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist have definitely not got any &quot;of the east&quot; vibes, and while dead they don't get their life force form the living, which I think of as the fundamentals of kindred (it's all about the blood drinking).<br /> <br /> Geist is more like a follow on to Wraith the Oblivian (but I've never read Wraith), but you are playing a living ghost bound to your own body... Still lots of Underworld Shenanigans, but you get to celebrate life, be thankful for second chances, and make the most of what time you have left.<br /> <br /> In my mind the biggest difference is that Geist characters haven't been tortured in hell. They may know what the Underworld looks like, and not want to go there (because it sucks) but they are oh so human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T15:11:10-08:00","id":1531253,"title":"","content":"My personal headcanon for a Kuei Jin like splat in CofD is indeed using the Lower Depths in general as an origin- souls who were already tainted by the Depths and, after death, were dragged to one of the many Hells which lurk below the world instead of following the regular progression of souls, getting pieces of themselves eaten by them in the process, only that through strong strength of will or some similar mystical occurrence have managed to claw their way back to the world of the living and reclaim their dead bodies, and now need to feed on souls to fill the pieces which were eaten from them by the Depths.<br /> <br /> So something which combine elements from Vampire, Mage and Mummy as a base setting for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}